WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.300
Morning, in a small shop. Piotr does not know the shopkeeper well.

2
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.090
Dzień dobry.

3
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.020
Dzień dobry.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.450
This greeting is polite. It works with people you do not know well.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.160
Do widzenia.

6
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.790
Do widzenia.

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.740
Goodbye. Polite, too.

8
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.990
In the park, Piotr meets his friend Ola.

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.680
Cześć!

10
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.230
Cześć!

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.420
With friends and family, the greeting is informal.

12
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.170
Na razie!

13
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.720
Cześć!

14
00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.150
The same informal word says hello and goodbye.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.960
Evening. The shopkeeper is closing up.

16
00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.950
Dobry wieczór.

17
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.780
Dobry wieczór.

18
00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.730
In the evening, the polite greeting changes.

19
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.020
Late at night, at home. Time to sleep.

20
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.990
Dobranoc.

21
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.740
Dobranoc.

22
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.850
Good night is for going to sleep, not for every goodbye.

23
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.560
The choice depends on how formal the situation is.

24
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.560
Polite, during the day.

25
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.470
Polite, in the evening.

26
00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.740
Informal, with friends and family.

27
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.660
Morning. Piotr walks into a shop. What does he say?

28
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.200
Dzień dobry.

29
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.560
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

30
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.400
Dzień dobry.

31
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.360
His friend Ola waves. What does Piotr say?

32
00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:58.860
Cześć!

33
00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.220
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

34
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.020
Cześć!

35
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.900
It is evening. He greets the shopkeeper. What does he say?

36
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.640
Dobry wieczór.

37
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.000
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

38
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.040
Dobry wieczór.

39
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.280
He leaves the shop. What does he say?

40
00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.940
Do widzenia.

41
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.300
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

42
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.260
Do widzenia.

43
00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.780
